        {
          "chunk_id": "med-chunk-a43cb96d1bc187e62f78",
          "document_id": "med-doc-b842fa97d1ec8758d0ec",
          "domain": "medical",
          "text": "puts you at a higher risk of getting type 2 diabetes. Over time, having too much glucose in your blood can cause serious problems. It can damage your eyes, kidneys, and nerves. Diabetes can also cause heart disease, stroke and even the need to remove a limb. Pregnant women can also get diabetes, called gestational diabetes. Blood tests can show if you have diabetes. One type of test, the A1C, can also check on how you are managing your diabetes. Exercise, weight control and sticking to your meal plan can help control your diabetes. You should also monitor your blood glucose level and take medicine if prescribed. NIH: National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases",
          "score": 0.012289162092274191,
          "source_url": "https://github.com/abachaa/MedQuAD/tree/577bd37b96c02d1833b2c9eed2de9f96964e96cb",
          "locator": "med-doc-b842fa97d1ec8758d0ec/med-chunk-a43cb96d1bc187e62f78",
          "text_sha256": "b548324612f9d86d65f9964556b4a53c5780a3373f06e6edb78f809caad891fc",
          "source_sha256": "42f025f955852567436dc7cd7efde701ca014429f47dacae7d7c0ba23ab51f29",
          "graph_path": [
            "kg-node-fcb21efed59ffe4ef1ceac5c",
            "med-chunk-a43cb96d1bc187e62f78"
          ]
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "med-chunk-4f099ecb0ff814fae6ce",
          "document_id": "med-doc-c92e281718761fee3d34",
          "domain": "medical",
          "text": "The two most common forms of diabetes are type 1 and type 2. Currently, there is no way to delay or prevent type 1 diabetes. However, research has shown that type 2 diabetes can be prevented or delayed in people at risk for the disease. Preventing type 2 diabetes can mean a healthier and longer life without serious complications from the disease such as heart disease, stroke, blindness, kidney failure, and amputations. Preventing Type 2 Diabetes Before people develop type 2 diabetes, they usually have prediabetes -- a condition in which blood glucose levels are higher than normal, but not yet high enough for a diagnosis of diabetes. The good news is that if you have prediabetes, there are ways",
          "score": 0.011701456063537317,
          "source_url": "https://github.com/abachaa/MedQuAD/tree/577bd37b96c02d1833b2c9eed2de9f96964e96cb",
          "locator": "med-doc-c92e281718761fee3d34/med-chunk-4f099ecb0ff814fae6ce",
          "text_sha256": "dfd99458efaea068809bcbc1d70fee02eb99efa026b14093578d28a2914682e9",
          "source_sha256": "42f025f955852567436dc7cd7efde701ca014429f47dacae7d7c0ba23ab51f29",
          "graph_path": [
            "kg-node-fcb21efed59ffe4ef1ceac5c",
            "med-chunk-4f099ecb0ff814fae6ce"
          ]
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "med-chunk-791eb61fb7e725fe87ee",
          "document_id": "med-doc-123d4ee06aa94a9f6267",
          "domain": "medical",
          "text": "the baby is born, a woman who has had it and her child are more likely to develop diabetes later in life. Prediabetes Prediabetes means your blood glucose levels are higher than normal but not high enough for a diagnosis of diabetes. People with prediabetes are at an increased risk for developing type 2 diabetes and for heart disease and stroke. The good news is that if you have prediabetes, you can reduce your risk of getting type 2 diabetes. With modest weight loss and moderate physical activity, you can delay or prevent type 2 diabetes. Learn more about prediabetes here. Signs of Diabetes Many people with diabetes experience one or more symptoms, including extreme thirst or hunger, a frequent",
          "score": 0.01155994043186895,
          "source_url": "https://github.com/abachaa/MedQuAD/tree/577bd37b96c02d1833b2c9eed2de9f96964e96cb",
          "locator": "med-doc-123d4ee06aa94a9f6267/med-chunk-791eb61fb7e725fe87ee",
          "text_sha256": "1fa8db623057a8ba52fddb9b4c5e973e454b83161cb72a5b4ef4ba36bd9e0491",
          "source_sha256": "42f025f955852567436dc7cd7efde701ca014429f47dacae7d7c0ba23ab51f29",
          "graph_path": [
            "kg-node-fcb21efed59ffe4ef1ceac5c",
