          ]
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "med-chunk-d4240633c83ab71e8998",
          "document_id": "med-doc-cbd2d980cea7901e8035",
          "domain": "medical",
          "text": "disease, and amputations. Other complications of diabetes may include increased susceptibility to other diseases, loss of mobility with aging, depression, and pregnancy problems. Main Types of Diabetes The three main types of diabetes are type 1, type 2, and gestational diabetes: - Type 1 diabetes, formerly called juvenile diabetes, is usually first diagnosed in children, teenagers, and young adults. In this type of diabetes, the beta cells of the pancreas no longer make insulin because the bodys immune system has attacked and destroyed them. - Type 2 diabetes, formerly called adult-onset diabetes, is the most common type of diabetes. About 90 to 95 percent of people with diabetes have type 2.1 People can develop type 2 diabetes at any age,",
          "score": 0.011264720942140297,
          "source_url": "https://github.com/abachaa/MedQuAD/tree/577bd37b96c02d1833b2c9eed2de9f96964e96cb",
          "locator": "med-doc-cbd2d980cea7901e8035/med-chunk-d4240633c83ab71e8998",
          "text_sha256": "166af6a70782b1a777fd1fb4ab6e6ef6241258ef007f9a616d154f9a6c1ca551",
          "source_sha256": "42f025f955852567436dc7cd7efde701ca014429f47dacae7d7c0ba23ab51f29",
          "graph_path": []
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "med-chunk-07f0e7ddf3090a20cda9",
          "document_id": "med-doc-9f6ec0d9f0125b5011cd",
          "domain": "medical",
          "text": "Diabetes is a very serious disease. Over time, diabetes that is not well managed causes serious damage to the eyes, kidneys, nerves, and heart, gums and teeth. If you have diabetes, you are more likely than someone who does not have diabetes to have heart disease or a stroke. People with diabetes also tend to develop heart disease or stroke at an earlier age than others. The best way to protect yourself from the serious complications of diabetes is to manage your blood glucose, blood pressure, and cholesterol and avoid smoking. It is not always easy, but people who make an ongoing effort to manage their diabetes can greatly improve their overall health.",
          "score": 0.011138861138861138,
          "source_url": "https://github.com/abachaa/MedQuAD/tree/577bd37b96c02d1833b2c9eed2de9f96964e96cb",
